# =============================================================================
# Lead Capture Pro — backup VPS authorized_keys (EXAMPLE, B23 G-6D C1/C2)
# =============================================================================
# Two local accounts on the BACKUP VPS, THREE key pairs, each with exactly ONE
# forced command. `restrict` disables PTY allocation, agent, X11 and TCP
# forwarding and user rc files; the client's requested command is handed to
# the forced command in SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND and parsed as the two-verb
# LCP-OFFHOST/1 protocol — a shell is never reachable.
#
# Key pairs (public keys only ever appear here; no real key is generated by
# the repository; replace the <…> placeholders during activation):
#   1. primary-to-backup UPLOAD key  — private key: primary VPS deploy user
#      ~/.ssh/lcp_offhost_upload_ed25519 (0600)
#   2. primary-to-backup AUDIT key   — private key: primary VPS deploy user
#      ~/.ssh/lcp_offhost_audit_ed25519 (0600)
#   3. GitHub-to-backup AUDIT key    — private key: ONLY the GitHub Actions
#      secret BACKUP_VPS_AUDIT_SSH_KEY; never installed on either VPS
# Keys 2 and 3 are bound to the same read-only audit command but are separate
# key pairs: each can be revoked and attributed on its own (sshd logs the
# fingerprint; the comment field names the holder). offhost-install-check.sh
# enforces this inventory EXACTLY: one receive key, two audit keys, every line
# `restrict,command="…"` with no other option, a supported ed25519 type whose
# decoded blob carries that type, and three DISTINCT fingerprints (a reused or
# duplicated key fails; comments alone never count as distinct keys).
#
# /home/lcp-receive/.ssh/authorized_keys   (owner lcp-receive:lcp-receive, mode 0600; ~/.ssh mode 0700)
restrict,command="/opt/lcp-offhost/bin/offhost-receive.sh" ssh-ed25519 <UPLOAD-PUBLIC-KEY-BASE64> lcp-offhost-upload@primary

# /home/lcp-audit/.ssh/authorized_keys     (owner lcp-audit:lcp-audit, mode 0600; ~/.ssh mode 0700)
restrict,command="/opt/lcp-offhost/bin/offhost-audit.sh" ssh-ed25519 <PRIMARY-AUDIT-PUBLIC-KEY-BASE64> lcp-offhost-audit@primary
restrict,command="/opt/lcp-offhost/bin/offhost-audit.sh" ssh-ed25519 <GITHUB-AUDIT-PUBLIC-KEY-BASE64> lcp-offhost-audit@github-actions

# /home/lcp-vault/.ssh/authorized_keys     MUST NOT EXIST (the vault identity has no SSH login)

# sshd_config on the backup VPS (activation prerequisite; the checker verifies
# the EFFECTIVE configuration globally with `sshd -T` AND per restricted
# account with `sshd -T -C user=lcp-receive,…` / `user=lcp-audit,…`, so a
# `Match User` block re-enabling passwords for one account is caught; every
# Match block may use the User criterion only, Includes must stay inside
# sshd_config.d, and the three service accounts must have locked passwords):
#   PasswordAuthentication no
#   KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
#   PubkeyAuthentication yes
#   PermitRootLogin no
#   AllowUsers lcp-receive lcp-audit <operator-account>   (never lcp-vault)
